  "knownIssues": [
    "Experimental: it has been built and tested without the games, but not yet run inside them.",
    "Leave Cities: Skylines' window open and not minimised: it's what draws the skyline.",
    "Go somewhere with open sky in RE2 (the police station's front gate and courtyard, the streets) to see your city.",
    "If the towers drift as you turn, change \"RE2 vertical FOV override\" in ReShade's RaccoonSkylines settings (Home key).",
    "If turning left in RE2 turns the city right, untick Mirror Z in Cities: Skylines' Raccoon City Skylines options.",
    "Kill and Mr. X events may not fire on every RE2 version; the rest still works.",
    "The first start of Cities: Skylines after installing compiles the mod, which takes a little longer."
  ],
  "important": [
    {
      "text": "In Cities: Skylines, open Content Manager, then Mods, and tick Raccoon City Skylines. Then load a city that has at least one police station.",
      "blocksInstall": false
    },
    {
      "text": "In Resident Evil 2's Graphics options, set Rendering mode to DirectX 11.",
      "blocksInstall": false
    }
  ]
